TOGGLE / App-default — honest coverage note (NOT a broken bidirectional gate)
  Row : "App view toggle (Axis 1 default) — boots to the schematic-default
        surface — no blueprint mounted eagerly."
  It asserts renderToStaticMarkup(<App/>) contains neither 'bp-svg' nor
  'View: Schematic'. LIMITATION, stated plainly: in the node env the store's
  async bundled-docs provider never resolves, so App SSR returns the
  `catalog.status === "initializing"` boot line ("<p class=boot>Loading…</p>",
  28 chars) — the solved block, the toggle button, and both view leaves are
  UNREACHABLE headless. This row therefore gates only that (a) App with the new
  wiring mounts without crashing and (b) the default view never eagerly mounts
  Blueprint into the boot path. It is NOT a strong bidirectional gate on the
  toggle's label/swap logic — flipping the App default to "blueprint" leaves SSR
  output unchanged (still the boot line), so no mutation of the default can fail
  this row. The toggle swap + label logic is inline JSX in App's solved block;
  its true gate is the team-lead browser walk (Axis 4, the pinned visual gate),
  same posture the GraphCanvas smoke exclusion already documents. The zero-
  machine empty-state gate (FAMILY 5) IS a real bidirectional check on
  Blueprint's own branch selection.

RESULT: all five production families are genuinely covered — each mutation
produced a FAIL naming the intended new assertion, and every restore returned
the suite to 377 green + check clean. Toggle-default coverage is smoke-only by
the SSR posture, documented above rather than faked.
